  <TabItem label="React Native (Cross-Platform)">

### Step 1: Install Node.js 20 LTS via FNM (Fast Node Manager)

We recommend **FNM** over NVM because it is built in Rust, loads 40x faster, and handles shell integration seamlessly:

```bash
# Install FNM and Watchman file observer
brew install fnm watchman

# Configure FNM in ~/.zshrc
echo 'eval "$(fnm env --use-on-cd)"' >> ~/.zshrc
source ~/.zshrc

# Install and activate Node.js 20 LTS
fnm install 20
fnm use 20
fnm default 20

# Verify versions
node -v   # Expected: v20.x.x
npm -v    # Expected: 10.x.x
```

### Step 2: Unified Toolchain Setup (Android & iOS Combined)

React Native projects compile to both platforms. Ensure you complete:
1. **Android Setup:** OpenJDK 17, `ANDROID_HOME`, and `platform-tools` (from the Android Tab).
2. **iOS Setup:** Xcode 16, Command Line Tools, and CocoaPods (from the iOS Tab).

Add the combined environment block to your `~/.zshrc`:

```bash
cat << 'EOF' >> ~/.zshrc

# Java 17 for React Native Android compilation
export JAVA_HOME="/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home"

# Android SDK
export ANDROID_HOME="$HOME/Library/Android/sdk"
export PATH="$PATH:$ANDROID_HOME/emulator"
export PATH="$PATH:$ANDROID_HOME/platform-tools"
export PATH="$PATH:$ANDROID_HOME/cmdline-tools/latest/bin"

# CocoaPods & Homebrew paths
export PATH="/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH"

EOF

source ~/.zshrc
```

### Step 3: Run the Enterprise Doctor Diagnostic CLI

Run the automated Doctor toolchain checker to verify your dual-platform setup:

```bash
# Execute workstation check
npx @enterprise/doctor-cli check

# Expected validation output:
# [PASS] Node.js 20.x detected
# [PASS] Watchman 2024.x detected
# [PASS] Xcode Command Line Tools (/Applications/Xcode.app)
# [PASS] CocoaPods installed
# [PASS] OpenJDK 17 installed
# [PASS] ANDROID_HOME configured
# [PASS] adb connected to local platform-tools
```

### Step 4: Boot Your First Starter Application

```bash
# Clone the enterprise React Native starter repository
git clone git@github.enterprise.com:mobile-starters/react-native-starter.git my-app
cd my-app

# Install project dependencies
npm install

# Install iOS CocoaPod native dependencies
cd ios && pod install && cd ..

# Boot the app on iOS Simulator
npm run ios

# Boot the app on Android Emulator (ensure AVD is started)
npm run android
```

