## Apple Silicon MacBook Troubleshooting

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">M-SERIES (ARM64) MACBOOK TIPS</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Android Emulator Acceleration:</strong> On Apple Silicon (M1/M2/M3/M4), do <em>not</em> attempt to install Intel HAXM. The Android Emulator uses Apple's native Hypervisor.framework out of the box. Always select the <code>arm64-v8a</code> ABI system image.</li>
    <li><strong>Homebrew Binary Path:</strong> Homebrew installs to <code>/opt/homebrew/bin</code> on Apple Silicon and <code>/usr/local/bin</code> on Intel. Never copy `~/.zshrc` files from an Intel Mac without adjusting paths.</li>
    <li><strong>Rosetta 2 for Legacy Pods:</strong> If an older third-party pod fails with an architecture compilation error, install Rosetta 2: <code>softwareupdate --install-rosetta --agree-to-license</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Node.js Architecture Mismatch:</strong> If you see `mach-o file, but is an incompatible architecture`, verify that your Node binary is native ARM64: <code>node -p "process.arch"</code> should return <code>arm64</code>.</li>
  </ul>
